    rabadon: SILENT — silenced; the gate returns 0 before any rule runs
      silenced by: .rabadon/mode = silent (/tmp/f1e-c5.bnhtVw/proj/.rabadon/mode)
        next: rm /tmp/f1e-c5.bnhtVw/proj/.rabadon/mode
      read from: /tmp/f1e-c5.bnhtVw/proj/.rabadon/mode (present)
    GATE EXIT=0  BYTES=0
  $ rabadon off      <- the command the screen itself printed
    rabadon: SILENT — silenced; the gate returns 0 before any rule runs
      silenced by: .rabadon/mode = silent (/tmp/f1e-c5.bnhtVw/proj/.rabadon/mode)
        next: rm /tmp/f1e-c5.bnhtVw/proj/.rabadon/mode
      the mode underneath is now `watch`, but nothing is evaluated at all while the silencer above is in place.
  after running it, the SAME event through the SAME binary:
    GATE EXIT=0  BYTES=0

=== CELL 3: <RABADON_DIR>/mode = silent (machine layer, control) ===
    rabadon: SILENT — silenced; the gate returns 0 before any rule runs
      silenced by: mode = silent (/tmp/f1e-c5.uRTcbJ/rdir/mode)
        next: rabadon off
      read from: /tmp/f1e-c5.uRTcbJ/rdir/mode (present)
    GATE EXIT=0  BYTES=0
    rabadon: WATCH — recording what it WOULD have caught, touching nothing (`rabadon on` to act)
    GATE EXIT=0  BYTES=296

